  "summary": "rrs exfiltrates full-screen screenshots and host identifiers to a hardcoded Discord webhook on CLI start",
  "details": "On launch of the `rrs` CLI, a background thread uses `mss` to capture a full-screen screenshot and POSTs it, together with the machine's hostname, username, OS/release string, and external IP, to a hardcoded Discord webhook URL (`discord.com/api/webhooks/1549807268294303860/...`) embedded in the shipped module. The capture routine (`run_capture()`) is invoked automatically from `main()` with no user consent, no configuration option, and no relation to the package's advertised P2P chat functionality. The Discord webhook URL (including its embedded token) is bundled in the source and serves as the author-controlled collector for the exfiltrated data.",
